e boy so that he can move the  boat closer what they don't know is that  jaws was hanging around underneath the  flicka for most of the day  the change in the boat's motor brings  the shark to life causing it to follow  the boat towards shallower water and  towards the boy chief brodie moves into  the water a bit getting knocked back by  a wave as the boy reaches chest deep  water and tries moving further towards  the shore the fin of the shark appears  out of the water behind him  between the chief and the shark the boy  moves a little bit faster because he  knows something is wrong  in a stroke of luck chief brody gets the  boy first and jaws retreats deeper into  the water while this scene is tense it  does display the natural limitations of  the shark since he has to continuously  move forward in order to breathe he has  to avoid accidentally beaching himself  over  a mouthful of food so the shallower  areas were essentially off limits  forced to close the beaches again amity  has to come up with another solution in  a last-ditch effort they call in former  war veteran turned shark hunter named  sam  quint a man who takes the cliche swears  like a sailor to the extreme  i'd love for him to meet our cab driver  from it with a new ally came a new boat  and even with a bigger boat  jaws was unafraid to back down from a  challenge you're gonna need a bigger  boat  on quinn's boat orca they managed to  encounter jaws a total of three times  the first time is only a brief passing  the second time hooper hops into his  shark cage to see jaws underwater and  take some photos when he goes in he  takes an underwater weapon in case jaws  gets too close  on the initial pass jaws swims close  enough to the cage for hooper to run his  hand along the side  the interaction is peaceful until the  sounds of quint firing shots into the  water disturb the scene  once this happened jaws swims out a bit  before ramming himself into the cage  he manages to pry the bars apart with  his continued ramming the same technique  used against elephant seals and more  dangerous prey it seems that jaws didn't  truly feel threatened until the shots  were fired at him  the disturbance agitated him to some  degree and he associated it with a  strange cage floating nearby  the hooper in the novel isn't as  fortunate as his film counterpart  before he's able to use the weapon the  shark bites down on his torso in a  display of  graphic details jaws jumps out of the  water hooper's legs hanging out of one  side of his mouth and his head and arms  out the other  i guess mrs john never taught her son  any proper manners at the dinner table  with hooper dead quintet declares that  this hunt is no longer a matter of money  though he never speaks the reason it  seems clear that he's developed a  burning desire to kill it  even if he has to do it alone their  final encounter with jaws turns into a  storied hunt that the novel has led up  to  once they get to a specific area closer  to the shore jaws surfaces as if waiting  for them within a half hour quinton  brady managed to hook three harpoons  into him one by his fin another near his  stomach and one in the head  just above the right eye during this  jaws attempts to sink their boat by  ramming into it even taking a bite to  shake the boat  eventually jaws resorts to trying to  swim away for nearly three hours  dragging the vessel with him as he goes  when the barrels stop moving quince  takes them in close to lasso jaws tail  and attempt to hoist him up on the winch  but jaws turns in a last-ditch effort to  escape and crashes onto the deck and the  impact is enough to start sinking the  boat in a mad fit of fury quince takes  the harpoon and stabs the shark in the  gut  deep enough for blood to cover his  entire hand when jaws rolls back into  the water quint's leg gets caught in the  rope tethered to the harpoon and he's  pulled overboard  jaws is simply trying to get back into  the water just in order to breathe but  it causes quince to end up drowning from  his own slip up pretty brutal way to go  but not as much as the movie though roll  that [ __ ]  luckily for chief brody he doesn't need  a gun or an oxygen tank to save himself  in the end  jaws is merely a mortal shark and dies  from his injuries just before getting  the chance to take a bite out of brody  the last we see of jaws is him sinking  back towards the depths of the ocean  in the end jaws terrorized the people of  amity and their summer visitors for  nearly an entire month the six victims  taken were not the only way that the  creature wrecked havoc on citizens  though it potentially ruined the entire  summer season economy  making the upcoming winter more  difficult while the film shows jaws as a  ruthless killer the novel reveals a more  realistic depiction of a shark with some  tendencies that we can analyze and  understand and others that can still not  be explained hopefully this analysis  helps add a layer of reality behind the  ocean dwelling terror that is jaws and  by the way let me know what other  creatures you'd like to see covered here  on horror history or what franchise  you'd like to see me take on remember to  subscribe to cz's world for new horrors  every week ring the death bell for  notifications and i'll see you in the  next one assuming  we both survive
 

